<div class="stack stack--{{type}} layout-sample">
    <p>Stack adds vertical rhythm only where elements meet.</p>
    <p>
    <p>Stack is a primitive layout component that can be used to create consistent vertical spacing between elements in
        a layout. It can be used in both successive and recursive modes, depending on the desired spacing behavior.</p>
    <p>In successive mode:
    <div>
        <p>Stack applies spacing only between direct siblings, meaning that only elements that are directly adjacent to
            each
            other will have spacing applied.</p>
        <p>This is useful for creating a clean and organized layout where elements are clearly separated.</p>
    </div>

    </p>
    <p>In recursive mode:
    <div>
        <p>Stack applies spacing between all nested elements, regardless of their hierarchy.</p>
        <p>This means that even elements that are not direct siblings will have spacing applied between them.</p>
    </div>

    </p>
</div>